{"name":"Bethany","hex":"#cadbbd","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Bethany","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["The village where Jesus stayed before going to Jerusalem and being crucified.","The village where Lazarus, Mary and Martha lived (Bible, John 11 v. 1)"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Bethany"}],"entries":[{"title":"Bethany","blocks":[{"text":"Bethany, locally called in Arabic al-Eizariya or el-Aizariya, is a Palestinian town in the Jerusalem Governorate of Palestine, bordering East Jerusalem, in the West Bank. The name al-Eizariya refers to the New Testament figure Lazarus of Bethany, who according to the Gospel of John, was raised from the dead by Jesus in the town. The traditional site of the miracle, the Tomb of Lazarus, in the city is a place of pilgrimage."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3e/%D7%94%D7%A0%D7%95%D7%A3_%D7%9C%D7%9E%D7%AA%D7%97%D7%9D_%D7%90%D7%95%D7%92%D7%95%D7%A1%D7%98%D7%94_%D7%95%D7%99%D7%A7%D7%98%D7%95%D7%A8%D7%99%D7%94.jpg/330px-%D7%94%D7%A0%D7%95%D7%A3_%D7%9C%D7%9E%D7%AA%D7%97%D7%9D_%D7%90%D7%95%D7%92%D7%95%D7%A1%D7%98%D7%94_%D7%95%D7%99%D7%A7%D7%98%D7%95%D7%A8%D7%99%D7%94.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bethany","wikidata":"Q831190"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bc/Al-%27Aizeriyeh.jpg/500px-Al-%27Aizeriyeh.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bc/Al-%27Aizeriyeh.jpg/500px-Al-%27Aizeriyeh.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Al-Eizariya at the start of the 20th century","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AAl-'Aizeriyeh.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/95/Betania_-_Zuallart_Jean_-_1587.jpg/500px-Betania_-_Zuallart_Jean_-_1587.jpg?u